## Knowledge types

{{- if .HasPersona}}

### persona

A kind of user of the product. Content block `persona`:

- `description` (required): who they are and how they relate to the product.
- `goals`: what they try to achieve with the product.
- `capabilities`: what they can do in the product, as the repository shows it.
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasRequirement}}

### requirement

A business requirement the product satisfies or enforces. Content block `requirement`:

- `statement` (required): the requirement, as one sentence.
- `kind` (required): `business-rule` (a rule of the domain), `functional` (something the product lets users do) or `constraint` (a limit imposed on the product).
- `rationale`: why it exists, only if a source says so.
- `personas`: ids of the persona interpretations it concerns, from this same report.
{{- end}}

## Output contract

Print exactly one JSON object on stdout, and nothing after it. Its shape:

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "observations": [
    {
      "id": "o1",
      "statement": "A factual statement about what the repository contains.",
      "evidence": [
        {"path": "relative/path/from/repository/root.ext", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 14, "excerpt": "the exact text of lines 12 to 14"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "interpretations": [
{{- if .HasPersona}}
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "type": "persona",
      "title": "Short label",
      "statement": "What this interpretation claims, in one or two sentences.",
      "nature": "supported",
      "observations": ["o1"],
      "persona": {"description": "...", "goals": ["..."], "capabilities": ["..."]}
    }{{if .HasRequirement}},{{end}}
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasRequirement}}
    {
      "id": "i2",
      "type": "requirement",
      "title": "Short label",
      "statement": "What this interpretation claims.",
      "nature": "hypothesis",
      "observations": [],
      "requirement": {"statement": "...", "kind": "business-rule", "rationale": "", "personas": [{{if .HasPersona}}"i1"{{end}}]}
    }
{{- end}}
  ],
  "questions": [
    {"id": "q1", "question": "Something a human should settle.", "about": [{{if .HasPersona}}"i1"{{else}}"i2"{{end}}]}
  ]
}
```

Rules, checked by Raun without exception:

- Every observation cites at least one piece of evidence. `excerpt` must be the complete text of lines `start_line` to `end_line` (1-based, inclusive) of `path` at the analyzed commit. Never quote part of a line, never paraphrase. Whitespace differences are tolerated; anything else makes the evidence invalid.
- One piece of evidence spans at most {{.MaxLines}} lines. Cite the few lines that matter, not whole files.
- `nature` is `supported` when the interpretation rests on observations (list at least one), `hypothesis` when it is your inference (observations optional).
- Each interpretation carries exactly the content block of its `type`.
- Ids are short and unique across the report (`o1`, `i1`, `q1`…). References (`observations`, `personas`, `about`) use ids of this report.
- `about` may be empty for questions about the project as a whole.
- No other fields are accepted.
